  # Research on Flight or Plane with Tail Number SU-BND

  - SU-BND is a Gulfstream IV-SP (serial 1332) operated by the Egyptian Air
  Force. [](grok_

  - SU-BND was being serviced at Duncan Aviation's facility in Provo, Utah,
  arriving around

  - SU-BND's visit aligned with the Egyptian government's long-term maintenance
  contract wi

  - Flight tracking data shows SU-BND was stationary on the tarmac for an
  extended period, '

  - SU-BND reactivated its transponder on September 13, 2025, and departed for
  Goose Bay, Ci

  - SU-BND was visible on the tarmac at PVU on September 10, 2025. I]
  (grok_render_citation_

  - Duncan Aviation's Provo location specializes in tip-to-tail MRO for
  Gulfstream aircraft

  - SU-BND's visit to Provo was for routine maintenance rather than operational
  purposes. [

  - SU-BND is an Egyptian Government private jet in Provo, Utah, at the time of
  Charlie Kir

  - SU-BND turned on its transponder but did not depart on September 10, 2025.
